    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδεῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>used at a libation</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔλημα,
				μέλος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.79
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ς</span>. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος</span>) a piece of music used at
			libations, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.11
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				35a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδεῖος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>), ὁ, in
			metre, <i>spondee</i>, foot consisting of two long syllables used
			in melodies accompanying <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδαί</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				3.1
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.
			of the pulse <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ ἴσου</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Syn.Puls.</u>
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
